We might also recall that the ratio of areas of two similar triangles is equal to the square of the ratio of their sides. We already know that the ratio of the two triangles is $\frac{2\sqrt{3}}{3}=\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}$.
The calculator shows us that $\frac{1}{3}\sqrt{3}\approx .577$. Squaring this, we get $\frac{1}{9}\cdot 3=\boxed{\frac{1}{3}}$.
