By same argument, $\angle WYX = \angle YXZ \to \tan Z = \frac{WY}{WZ}$, so $WZ = \frac{WY}{\tan Z} = 12$. Likewise, $WY = WX$ and $WY = 12\tan X = 12\tan(180^\circ - 90^\circ) = 12\cot Z = 12 (\tan Z)^{-1} = 12(1/1.5) = 8$.

Then the area of trapezoid $WXYZ$ is $8(12+12)/2 = \boxed{96}$. </think> <answer> 96 </answer>

